Status: ACTIVE
Milestone: Ongoing causal development history
Dependencies: None
Purpose: Preserve what changed, why, evidence and unresolved boundaries.

Tasks:
- [x] Record initial emulator decision.
- [x] Append implementation and verification outcomes at milestones.

Acceptance criteria:
- Decisions, actual technical evidence, human approval and publication remain distinct.

Completion evidence:
- Verified upstream v4.2.3 source maps gba to mgba.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-03 / Foundation:
  Started from one README heading. Chose an established WebAssembly emulator
  rather than building a CPU emulator for a UI prototype. Pin 4.2.3 and use a
  small compatibility adapter: current docs include save hooks absent in the
  release loader. Own checked checkpoint persistence instead of relying on
  upstream storage methods that can swallow IndexedDB errors.
- 2026-11-04 / Implementation:
  Built a static vanilla-module shell, file validation/content identity, isolated
  iframe adapter, independent automatic/manual slots and versioned backups.
  Created original Pixel Lab ARM test program instead of using commercial ROM
  bytes. Initial mode-3 full-screen redraw raced scanout, hiding its moving
  square; changed to one initial fill plus bounded VBlank erase/redraw.
- 2026-11-04 / Integration failures and fixes:
  Runtime first threw because unused player maps were omitted; supply all four.
  Reload then restored reset progress despite working in-session restores.
  An initial two-frame acknowledgment change did not fix that reload regression.
  Native logs and pinned source exposed upstream beforeunload resetting the
  core, including cancelled navigation. Suppressing that child handler fixed
  reload; the host retains its own leave prompt.
  Touch initialization exposed a hidden-control setting and a zero-height
  absolute-positioned wrapper; use documented default options and verify the
  actual A button can be tapped, rather than the wrapper's geometry.
- 2026-11-04 / Verification:
  Final focused unit suite 5/5; real Edge browser suite 6/6; syntax/build pass.
  Browser evidence includes actual input, SRAM capture, manual restore,
  portable backup import/export, renamed-ROM reload, real interval capture,
  ROM isolation, failed storage writes/export recovery, mobile control tap and
  failed CDN load. Physical devices, commercial games and hearing audio remain
  unverified. Screenshots reviewed; no user approval inferred.
- 2026-11-04 / Pages:
  User supplied Actions-source Pages settings. API independently confirmed
  workflow configuration and https://zanark.github.io/BowserBoyAdvance/.
  Added check/build/browser-test gates and dist-only deploy workflow. No
  commit, push, dispatch or publication has been authorized/performed.
- 2026-11-04 / Publication authorization:
  User explicitly requested git add, commit and push after prototype completion.
  Deliver the existing locally verified prototype without bundling private
  context, dependencies or generated dist. A successful push is not itself
  proof of a successful hosted Actions run or live Pages deployment.
- 2026-11-04 / Published prototype and approval:
  Commit 8390832 reached origin/main; Actions run 41700230948 completed build
  and deploy successfully. User separately reported the prototype works and
  is good. Do not extend that approval to later design changes.
- 2026-11-04 / Hardware UI:
  User requested an actual-GBA aesthetic with no LCD buttons and Z=A/X=B.
  Clarified scope before implementation: retain functional physical shell
  buttons; move existing tools into a hidden drawer; add remapping and sound.
  Used original CSS geometry, texture and project-name typography, not copied
  photos, game artwork or a Nintendo logo. Retained all save/runtime identities.
- 2026-11-04 / Input and settings:
  Verified pinned simulateInput and setVolume internals before adapting them.
  Shared keyboard handling prevents native mappings bypassing a rebind. Track
  held sources separately so a pointer release cannot cancel a held key.
  Give short taps a minimum 40 ms pulse and release on cancel/lost capture/blur.
  Keep continuous inputs enabled while background checkpoint writes run.
  Checked preference writes report session-only recovery instead of claiming
  persistence. Keep sound settings distinct from evidence of audible playback.
- 2026-11-04 / Visual verification:
  An initial passing mobile test only hid the virtual-gamepad wrapper. Actual
  screenshot review exposed a separate native hamburger over the LCD. Pinned
  source identified ejs_virtualGamepad_open outside that wrapper; removed it
  and asserted its invisibility. Final real-core suite 9/9, unit suite 8/8,
  syntax and clean build pass. New UI acceptance/publication remain pending.
- 2026-11-04 / Actual 3D and native shader:
  User requested a real model on a table rather than another flat illustration.
  Confirmed one indigo handheld, original cartridge props, pickup/play/inspect/
  return and no default games yet. Chose original procedural Three.js geometry;
  package only pinned 0.186.1 modules and its full MIT license.
  Verified crt-geom.glslp in the actual 4.2.3 shader collection. A live probe
  established that preserveDrawingBuffer:false makes native canvas copies black.
  Disable engine auto-start, configure just its own canvas in EJS_ready, then
  activate the native start button. Retained post-shader frames now feed a
  CanvasTexture directly, without screenshots, flat iframe projection or a
  replacement CRT approximation.
- 2026-11-04 / 3D interaction and verification:
  Mesh raycasting picks up the handheld; inspection rotates its actual front,
  edges and back. Pointer/touch/pinch/wheel/keyboard interactions work, with
  reduced-motion pickup and explicit unavailable/lost graphics errors.
  Project transparent accessible inputs onto real button positions, keep them
  off the LCD, gate host/keyboard input outside play view and retain gamepads.
  The child marks its native canvas with an owned DOM contract, keeping engine
  globals out of the parent. Existing checkpoint and runtime identities remain.
  Initial visual review found small decals recessed behind beveled faces;
  corrected their surface depth. Native core context can be WebGL 1; the 3D
  renderer separately needs WebGL 2. Final syntax/build, 9 unit and 13 real Edge
  browser cases pass, including native CRT pixel differences and touch pinch.
  Only original Pixel Lab used; no stopped commercial-ROM test was restarted.
  User visual approval and new publication remain pending.
- 2026-11-04 / Reference correction:
  User rejected the initial shape and supplied Andy Dream's Sketchfab model.
  Public API reported no downloadable model and no listed reuse license.
  Used its visible proportions only: stepped upper crown/shoulders, straighter
  sides, bowed lower edge, smaller rounded controls and real recessed grille.
  Mesh/texture assets were not extracted; the thumbnail remains private.
  Corrected LCD recess occlusion, pivot-well floor and switch-grip depth.
  Actual raycast assertions protect those three front-surface relationships.
  Table/front/back renders reviewed; syntax/build, 9 units and final 13 browser
  cases pass. Two earlier reload PNG assertions failed; direct pixel probing
  and subsequent isolated/full runs passed without a production save change.
  The intermittent assertion's root cause remains unresolved. Original demo
  only; human visual acceptance and publication remain pending.
- 2026-11-04 / Real power lifecycle and release authorization:
  User requested actual off/on with ROM boot from in-game save, never an instant
  checkpoint. Retain the selected File only in memory; flush/commit battery
  memory separately, remove the iframe and blank the real LCD/LED. Power on
  creates a new runtime, loads only battery memory and restarts the ROM.
  Optional battery/bootMode record fields preserve existing database/backup
  versions and old checkpoint slots. An explicit power off suppresses stale
  checkpoint auto-resume after reload until a new checkpoint is captured.
  Pause remains a separate drawer action. Failed battery writes keep the game
  on for backup recovery. The first test found a status toast intercepting the
  projected switch; made its noninteractive body pointer-transparent.
  A globally denied IndexedDB fixture prevented the pinned core starting;
  retained that reporting test and separately simulated only app-store denial
  for session-only power-cycle coverage. Final syntax/build, 9 units and
  16 browser cases pass. User then explicitly authorized deploying everything;
  publish all completed public work, never private context or ROM bytes.
